# The rule: a declaration whose header was never included is diagnosed at the
# user .ccs coordinates of the declaration, not inside the generated C.
# The row calls cc_string_len directly rather than through UFCS `s.len()`.
# A UFCS receiver whose type is undeclared has no installed methods, so a
# lowerer that resolves UFCS against the index refuses the call first and the
# host compile never runs -- that is break_diag_ufcs_miss_fail's subject, and
# pinning it here made this row depend on a lowerer that guesses the family
# spelling and defers the whole question to the host.
break_diag_missing_include_fail.ccs:5:5
CCString
